meta {
  name: Vol-ST Replay
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/vol-st/replay
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~underlying: AAPL
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Option ST Alert — Intraday Replay (today's RTH)

  TRUE bar-by-bar replay of the option-vol-st Supertrend alert over TODAY's RTH session
  (09:30–16:00 ET). For each underlying it takes the stock's OPEN price (today's 09:30 bar),
  generates the near-the-money contracts (both sides) off that open, fetches each contract's
  max M1 bars, and walks them bar-by-bar — evaluating the legs on only the data up to each bar
  (no lookahead) and recording every fired signal with its timestamp. A `cooldown-minutes`
  period suppresses re-fires on the same contract after a fire.

  ## Query
  - `underlying` — optional; scope to one symbol. Omit for all configured underlyings.

  ## Response (200)
  {
    date, session, timeframe, stRisingCandles, emaPeriod, emaAboveCandles, volumeEnabled,
    cooldownMinutes, totalSignals,
    results: [ { underlying, stockOpen, contractsWithSignals, signalCount,
                 contracts: [ { occSymbol, type, strike, moneyness, rthBars,
                                signals: [ { firedAtEt, optionClose, stRisingStreak,
                                             aboveEma, volumeOk } ] } ] } ]
  }

  ## Notes
  - Strikes are picked off the stock's OPEN price (what was ATM at the open), not the current
    price. Only contracts that fired at least once are listed.
  - Options have no deep dated history (most-recent-N bars), so ONLY today's RTH session is
    replayable; older dates can't be reconstructed.
}
